WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.524
JAMIE: In plain terms — you train
the model

00:00:02.524 --> 00:00:05.048
JAMIE: on matching pairs. This
structure goes with this

00:00:05.048 --> 00:00:07.571
JAMIE: description. That structure
does not go with that

00:00:07.571 --> 00:00:10.095
JAMIE: description. Over time it
develops a shared language

00:00:10.095 --> 00:00:12.619
JAMIE: between the atomic picture
and the prose.

00:00:12.729 --> 00:00:15.001
RUFUS: It's a bit like teaching
someone to recognize

00:00:15.001 --> 00:00:17.272
RUFUS: wine by pairing the taste
with the vocabulary,

00:00:17.272 --> 00:00:19.544
RUFUS: rather than teaching each
separately.

00:00:19.609 --> 00:00:21.386
JAMIE: That's actually a good
analogy.

00:00:21.566 --> 00:00:22.877
RUFUS: I have them occasionally.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.167
ALEX: Don't tell him that.

00:00:24.232 --> 00:00:27.005
RUFUS: I already was insufferable.
This changes nothing.
